WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:13.375 --> 00:00:16.893
I'm here to honor the sacredness of life

00:00:16.917 --> 00:00:20.268
that I see at the border in south Texas.

00:00:20.292 --> 00:00:22.768
In 2014,

00:00:22.792 --> 00:00:25.559
I visited a detention facility

00:00:25.583 --> 00:00:29.768
where hundreds of little children,

00:00:29.792 --> 00:00:31.101
immigrant children,

00:00:31.125 --> 00:00:33.684
were detained for several weeks

00:00:33.708 --> 00:00:37.309
in conditions that were
very heartbreaking.

00:00:37.333 --> 00:00:40.101
They were dirty and muddy

00:00:40.125 --> 00:00:41.375
and crying.

00:00:42.333 --> 00:00:45.208
Their faces were full of tears.

00:00:46.042 --> 00:00:49.875
I had the opportunity to go in
and be with them.

00:00:51.250 --> 00:00:53.309
And they were all around me.

00:00:53.333 --> 00:00:57.268
They were little ones,

00:00:57.292 --> 00:01:00.750
some of them not older
than five years old.

00:01:01.875 --> 00:01:04.476
And they were saying to me,

00:01:04.500 --> 00:01:06.518
(Spanish) "Sácame de aquí."

00:01:06.542 --> 00:01:07.917
"Get me out of here."

00:01:09.708 --> 00:01:11.309
(Spanish) "Por favor, ayúdame."

00:01:11.333 --> 00:01:12.625
"Please, help me."

00:01:13.875 --> 00:01:17.018
It was so difficult to be there with them.

00:01:17.042 --> 00:01:18.851
I started to cry with them,

00:01:18.875 --> 00:01:20.792
and I told them,

00:01:21.667 --> 00:01:22.934
"Let us pray."

00:01:22.958 --> 00:01:24.768
(Spanish) "Vamos a rezar."

00:01:24.792 --> 00:01:26.583
And they repeated after me,

00:01:27.458 --> 00:01:30.226
(Spanish) "Diosito, ayúdanos."

00:01:30.250 --> 00:01:32.375
"God, please, help us."

00:01:33.542 --> 00:01:37.143
As we prayed, I could see
the Border Patrol officers

00:01:37.167 --> 00:01:39.250
looking through a glass window.

00:01:40.500 --> 00:01:42.625
They were at the verge of tears.

00:01:43.833 --> 00:01:46.875
As they heard the children
praying and witness.

00:01:47.708 --> 00:01:51.851
I had a little boy
get close to me, closer,

00:01:51.875 --> 00:01:53.518
because they were all over,

00:01:53.542 --> 00:01:56.375
we could barely fit in that little cell.

00:01:57.583 --> 00:02:00.184
And this little boy tells me,

00:02:00.208 --> 00:02:02.268
(Spanish) "Ayúdame.

00:02:02.292 --> 00:02:04.434
Quiero irme con mi mamá."

00:02:04.458 --> 00:02:06.018
"Please, help me.

00:02:06.042 --> 00:02:07.976
I want to be with my mother.

00:02:08.000 --> 00:02:11.333
She is here, I was separated from her."

00:02:12.625 --> 00:02:14.184
I said to him,

00:02:14.208 --> 00:02:16.809
"Mijo, if your mom is here,

00:02:16.833 --> 00:02:19.583
I'm certain you will be reunited."

00:02:21.417 --> 00:02:23.500
When I walked out of the cell,

00:02:24.833 --> 00:02:27.768
an officer got close to me and said to me,

00:02:27.792 --> 00:02:29.375
"Sister, thank you.

00:02:30.292 --> 00:02:32.875
You have helped us realize

00:02:34.417 --> 00:02:35.875
that they are human beings."

00:02:37.792 --> 00:02:40.684
You know, sometimes,
no matter what job we have,

00:02:40.708 --> 00:02:44.184
we must never forget to recognize

00:02:44.208 --> 00:02:46.976
the humanity in others.

00:02:47.000 --> 00:02:49.625
Otherwise, we will lose our own humanity.

00:02:51.292 --> 00:02:54.768
Let me tell you a bit
about what I see and what I do

00:02:54.792 --> 00:02:57.309
in the southern border
of the United States

00:02:57.333 --> 00:02:59.875
where I live and where I work.

00:03:01.167 --> 00:03:04.684
Hundreds of families
enter the United States

00:03:04.708 --> 00:03:07.083
by crossing the Rio Grande river.

00:03:07.917 --> 00:03:10.518
And once they are in the United States,

00:03:10.542 --> 00:03:12.184
many of them are given permission

00:03:12.208 --> 00:03:15.226
to continue their process of immigration

00:03:15.250 --> 00:03:18.434
at another point in the United States.

00:03:18.458 --> 00:03:21.684
What has amazed me for all these years

00:03:21.708 --> 00:03:26.643
has been the amazing humanitarian response

00:03:26.667 --> 00:03:29.250
of the community there in south Texas.

00:03:30.333 --> 00:03:32.393
Thousands of volunteers

00:03:32.417 --> 00:03:35.893
have given of their time so generously.

00:03:35.917 --> 00:03:38.917
For me, they're all amazing people.

00:03:39.833 --> 00:03:41.851
And the whole community,

00:03:41.875 --> 00:03:43.476
city government,

00:03:43.500 --> 00:03:46.351
from local business leaders

00:03:46.375 --> 00:03:48.434
to civic organizations,

00:03:48.458 --> 00:03:50.518
all faith communities,

00:03:50.542 --> 00:03:52.851
in the Border Patrol and ICE.

00:03:52.875 --> 00:03:56.601
We have all come together
in an effort to help

00:03:56.625 --> 00:04:02.851
150,000 or more immigrants
since that first day that we got started.

00:04:02.875 --> 00:04:04.476
Back in those first days

00:04:04.500 --> 00:04:08.268
when we were first involved
in helping the immigrants,

00:04:08.292 --> 00:04:10.268
we were at our respite center,

00:04:10.292 --> 00:04:13.226
and an officer from the city walks in

00:04:13.250 --> 00:04:15.559
and tells me,

00:04:15.583 --> 00:04:18.458
"Sister, what are you doing here?"

00:04:19.500 --> 00:04:22.226
I turned and looked
to see what was happening

00:04:22.250 --> 00:04:23.833
at the respite center.

00:04:24.792 --> 00:04:27.393
I was amazed at what I was seeing.

00:04:27.417 --> 00:04:30.184
There were hundreds of volunteers

00:04:30.208 --> 00:04:35.184
helping so many families there
that needed help.

00:04:35.208 --> 00:04:38.643
Giving them ways to get cleaned up

00:04:38.667 --> 00:04:42.309
and to get clean clothing, food,

00:04:42.333 --> 00:04:44.476
hygiene items.

00:04:44.500 --> 00:04:49.518
Just love and compassion
was seen everywhere.

00:04:49.542 --> 00:04:53.726
So I turned back and I responded
to him and I said,

00:04:53.750 --> 00:04:56.393
"Restoring human dignity.

00:04:56.417 --> 00:04:58.351
That's what we're doing."

00:04:58.375 --> 00:05:00.809
I don't think he expected
that answer from me,

00:05:00.833 --> 00:05:02.226
because he took a step back

00:05:02.250 --> 00:05:05.226
and then approached me again and said,

00:05:05.250 --> 00:05:09.601
"Sister, if I had a magic wand,

00:05:09.625 --> 00:05:11.833
what would that magic wand do for you?"

00:05:12.917 --> 00:05:14.351
"Showers?"

00:05:14.375 --> 00:05:18.458
Sure enough, that evening
we had a mobile unit of eight showers.

00:05:19.542 --> 00:05:20.809
Amazing.

00:05:20.833 --> 00:05:22.101
And after that,

00:05:22.125 --> 00:05:25.726
we had 100 percent support
of the city government.

00:05:25.750 --> 00:05:27.059
We were there,

00:05:27.083 --> 00:05:29.893
wanting to make sure that we were helping

00:05:29.917 --> 00:05:31.809
and be successful with our response

00:05:31.833 --> 00:05:34.143
to so many families that we were seeing

00:05:34.167 --> 00:05:36.018
every single day.

00:05:36.042 --> 00:05:40.309
I think that we must help others see

00:05:40.333 --> 00:05:42.226
what we see.

00:05:42.250 --> 00:05:44.143
I think it's important

00:05:44.167 --> 00:05:46.500
that we can share that with others.

00:05:48.042 --> 00:05:50.559
You probably heard this idea before --

00:05:50.583 --> 00:05:55.792
that we must always see
God's children as equal.

00:05:56.708 --> 00:05:57.976
But in order to do that,

00:05:58.000 --> 00:06:02.851
I think it's important
to be able to see them

00:06:02.875 --> 00:06:04.125
as people.

00:06:05.250 --> 00:06:07.684
To be able to have a personal encounter,

00:06:07.708 --> 00:06:09.726
when we can feel what they feel,

00:06:09.750 --> 00:06:12.292
when we can understand
what they're hurting.

00:06:13.708 --> 00:06:15.583
To really meet up with them.

00:06:17.208 --> 00:06:19.309
It is then that we are present to them

00:06:19.333 --> 00:06:22.143
and we can make their humanity

00:06:22.167 --> 00:06:24.601
a part of our own humanity.

00:06:24.625 --> 00:06:26.268
And we'd recognize

00:06:26.292 --> 00:06:29.250
that we are all part
of the same human family.

00:06:29.958 --> 00:06:32.101
During those days,

00:06:32.125 --> 00:06:35.559
I had a lady approach me and tell me,

00:06:35.583 --> 00:06:40.559
"Sister, I am 100 percent
against what you do,

00:06:40.583 --> 00:06:42.809
helping these illegal aliens."

00:06:42.833 --> 00:06:44.434
And I said to her,

00:06:44.458 --> 00:06:47.875
"Let me tell you what I do and why."

00:06:49.208 --> 00:06:53.643
So I shared with her and introduced her
to the families and the children,

00:06:53.667 --> 00:06:56.393
shared the stories that they are living.

00:06:56.417 --> 00:06:59.309
When I finished talking with her,

00:06:59.333 --> 00:07:01.893
she turns and looks at me and says,

00:07:01.917 --> 00:07:06.726
"Sister, I am 100 percent
in favor of what you do."

00:07:06.750 --> 00:07:12.101
(Laughter and applause)

00:07:12.125 --> 00:07:14.559
That evening, her husband calls me,

00:07:14.583 --> 00:07:15.851
he tells me,

00:07:15.875 --> 00:07:18.851
"Sister, I don't know
what you did to my wife.

00:07:18.875 --> 00:07:21.976
But this evening
she came home and she said,

00:07:22.000 --> 00:07:23.893
'If Sister Norma ever calls you,

00:07:23.917 --> 00:07:26.476
you make sure you do what she tells you.'

00:07:26.500 --> 00:07:30.000
So I'm just reporting to let you know
I'm here to help in any way."

00:07:30.917 --> 00:07:32.167
Well, you know ...

00:07:34.375 --> 00:07:36.059
I'm thinking that --

00:07:36.083 --> 00:07:38.750
was it a personal encounter that she had?

00:07:39.667 --> 00:07:42.309
I think it's a nice idea, a nice message,

00:07:42.333 --> 00:07:45.268
but I don't think it's the whole story.

00:07:45.292 --> 00:07:51.268
In that encounter, we must put aside
our prejudice that we have toward others,

00:07:51.292 --> 00:07:54.976
that separate us
and don't allow us to see them,

00:07:55.000 --> 00:07:57.726
our walls that we put up in our own heart

00:07:57.750 --> 00:08:00.333
that keep us separated from others.

00:08:01.000 --> 00:08:03.476
When we are able to do that,

00:08:03.500 --> 00:08:06.000
we're able to reach out to them.

00:08:06.833 --> 00:08:12.018
You know, I think what
doesn't make it possible is fear --

00:08:12.042 --> 00:08:13.643
that we're afraid.

00:08:13.667 --> 00:08:15.518
And because we're afraid --

00:08:15.542 --> 00:08:18.726
more than likely it's because
we've seen in the media

00:08:18.750 --> 00:08:22.601
all this negative rhetoric
that we hear about immigrants,

00:08:22.625 --> 00:08:25.768
they are demonized,
like they're not human,

00:08:25.792 --> 00:08:27.768
that we can discard them

00:08:27.792 --> 00:08:29.226
and we can get rid of them,

00:08:29.250 --> 00:08:31.768
and not even feel bad
that we're doing that.

00:08:31.792 --> 00:08:34.500
Immigrant families are not criminals.

00:08:35.958 --> 00:08:39.601
Immigrant families are like our families,

00:08:39.625 --> 00:08:41.250
like our neighbors.

00:08:42.125 --> 00:08:43.893
They're good people

00:08:43.917 --> 00:08:47.643
who are entering our country
and coming to the United States

00:08:47.667 --> 00:08:50.518
only simply because they're fleeing
away from violence

00:08:50.542 --> 00:08:51.917
and they want to be safe.

00:08:53.042 --> 00:08:57.018
Unfortunately, what we see at the border

00:08:57.042 --> 00:08:58.851
is terrible.

00:08:58.875 --> 00:09:01.434
People are hurting and suffering.

00:09:01.458 --> 00:09:02.917
Thousands of them are.

00:09:03.750 --> 00:09:05.268
And mostly I feel

00:09:05.292 --> 00:09:07.976
it's because of those walls
that we put up,

00:09:08.000 --> 00:09:10.351
that we have in our hearts,

00:09:10.375 --> 00:09:12.518
that makes us not care.

00:09:12.542 --> 00:09:14.143
So we have policies

00:09:14.167 --> 00:09:16.768
that are returning people back to Mexico,

00:09:16.792 --> 00:09:18.143
so they can wait.

00:09:18.167 --> 00:09:20.167
And they wait there for months.

00:09:21.167 --> 00:09:23.226
In conditions that are horrible,

00:09:23.250 --> 00:09:25.292
where people are suffering and hurting.

00:09:26.417 --> 00:09:27.809
Abuses.

00:09:27.833 --> 00:09:31.125
And not even the means to be OK.

00:09:32.542 --> 00:09:35.458
I think that it is true

00:09:36.792 --> 00:09:39.542
that we must keep our country safe,

00:09:40.667 --> 00:09:44.351
that we must make sure
who enters our country,

00:09:44.375 --> 00:09:46.458
that criminals should be put away.

00:09:47.500 --> 00:09:49.809
But it is also true

00:09:49.833 --> 00:09:54.809
that we must not lose
our humanity in doing this.

00:09:54.833 --> 00:09:57.351
That we must have policies and procedures

00:09:57.375 --> 00:10:00.559
that do not contribute
to the human suffering

00:10:00.583 --> 00:10:03.268
that people are already suffering.

00:10:03.292 --> 00:10:08.018
And that we can find solutions
that are respectful to all human life.

00:10:08.042 --> 00:10:09.434
We can do this,

00:10:09.458 --> 00:10:12.726
if we can allow the best
in us to come out.

00:10:12.750 --> 00:10:15.601
Because what I see at the border

00:10:15.625 --> 00:10:20.768
are families, men, who will take a child

00:10:20.792 --> 00:10:24.768
and will try to comfort
that child that is crying

00:10:24.792 --> 00:10:27.851
because that child is crying
for their own dad.

00:10:27.875 --> 00:10:31.726
And these men are crying with that child.

00:10:31.750 --> 00:10:36.643
I see men and women
who drop to their knees,

00:10:36.667 --> 00:10:38.268
praying.

00:10:38.292 --> 00:10:40.833
As they pray in thanksgiving.

00:10:42.417 --> 00:10:47.018
I see children who have been separated
from their parents for months.

00:10:47.042 --> 00:10:48.476
And when they're reunited,

00:10:48.500 --> 00:10:51.393
they're afraid to separate
themselves from them,

00:10:51.417 --> 00:10:54.500
because they're afraid
they will lose their mom again.

00:10:55.542 --> 00:10:59.559
Once a child looked up to me
after she was reunited

00:10:59.583 --> 00:11:01.292
and she said to me,

00:11:02.292 --> 00:11:04.042
(Spanish) "Hoy no voy a llorar."

00:11:04.917 --> 00:11:06.518
"Today I'm not going to cry."

00:11:06.542 --> 00:11:08.559
And I said, (Spanish) "Por qué, mi hija?"

00:11:08.583 --> 00:11:12.542
She said, "Because I have been crying
for the past whole month,

00:11:13.708 --> 00:11:16.643
because I didn't know where my mother was.

00:11:16.667 --> 00:11:19.250
But tonight, I'm going to be with her."

00:11:20.583 --> 00:11:25.059
The day I visited the detention
facility back in 2014,

00:11:25.083 --> 00:11:28.292
there was a little boy
who approached me and asked me

00:11:29.917 --> 00:11:32.542
for me to help him find his mom.

00:11:33.833 --> 00:11:38.083
Well, that evening, when I was
at the humanitarian respite center,

00:11:39.042 --> 00:11:41.250
the little boy walked in with his mother.

00:11:42.500 --> 00:11:44.101
And as soon as he spotted me,

00:11:44.125 --> 00:11:46.643
he runs toward me, I go down to greet him,

00:11:46.667 --> 00:11:49.583
and he just throws himself to hug me.

00:11:50.875 --> 00:11:52.143
It was so beautiful,

00:11:52.167 --> 00:11:56.976
that was truly
a beautiful human encounter.

00:11:57.000 --> 00:12:00.250
I think it's humanity at its best.

00:12:01.167 --> 00:12:05.226
It is what we all are called to do.

00:12:05.250 --> 00:12:06.500
Think about it.

00:12:07.875 --> 00:12:13.125
We just need to allow ourselves
to get close enough to see,

00:12:13.958 --> 00:12:15.208
and we will care.

00:12:16.083 --> 00:12:17.351
Thank you.

00:12:17.375 --> 00:12:21.625
(Applause)

